// Scoped to the App target's Release configuration only (see baseConfigurationReference in
// App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj), mirroring the pattern proven in Let Them Eat Cake and Ramen.
// Deliberately NOT passed as xcodebuild command-line overrides in the release workflow, since
// those apply to every target in the build graph (including auto-generated SPM resource-bundle
// targets that can't be signed at all), and headless `xcodebuild archive` resolves Automatic
// signing to "development" purpose for every target regardless of the archive action. Scoping
// via xcconfig avoids both problems.
//
// *** NOT YET WIRED IN. This file is ready but two things are still required before it does
// anything: ***
// 1. The two placeholder values below must be replaced with this app's real Apple Developer
//    Team ID and the exact provisioning profile name once those exist in App Store Connect.
// 2. This file must be set as the Release configuration's base configuration on the App target
//    in Xcode (Project navigator -> App project -> App target -> Info tab -> Configurations ->
//    Release -> App -> select this file). That step requires Xcode and cannot be done from this
//    environment (no Xcode available here). See NATIVE_SETUP.md for the full walkthrough.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Distribution
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = J48FJJ3ABL
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER = Let Them Eat Noodles App Store
